# The dataset the plugin ships. Generated, and written minified by tools/fetch-data.mjs
# — one very long line per file, deliberately. Expanding it here would be undone the
# next time anybody reruns the fetch.
data/

# The landing page GitHub Pages serves, and the card it renders. Both are laid out by
# hand, and prettier's HTML mode rewrites them end to end — one attribute per line, the
# doctype lowercased — for nothing gained on a page nobody diffs.
docs/

# npm writes this one, and npm decides its shape.
package-lock.json

# The tables in here are aligned by eye. Prettier pads them by code point rather than by
# display width, so every row carrying an em dash or a ◓ comes out ragged in the source
# and no better in the render.
README.md

# Where CI points CLAUDEMON_HOME. Downloaded sprites, never source.
.claudemon-ci/
